WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.200 align:start position:0%
Your first fifteen seconds decide whether anyone stays.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:06.800 align:start position:0%
Most hooks fail because they summarise instead of opening a question.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:07.400 align:start position:0%
um

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:11.200 align:start position:0%
Here is the structure I use for every opening line now.

00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.900 align:start position:0%
Confirm the title, open a gap, then prove the payoff exists.

00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:19.800 align:start position:0%
If the opening line needs context it is not working yet.

00:00:19.900 --> 00:00:20.300 align:start position:0%
so yeah

00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:24.100 align:start position:0%
Read the hook out loud and stop where you run out of breath.

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:28.600 align:start position:0%
Read the hook out loud and stop where your breath runs out.

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.000 align:start position:0%
Thumbnails work at feed size or they do not work at all.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:38.700 align:start position:0%
Shrink every thumbnail down to a postage stamp before choosing.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:39.300 align:start position:0%
basically

00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:43.200 align:start position:0%
Three words maximum because a fourth word becomes a grey smear.

00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:47.100 align:start position:0%
The thumbnail should never repeat the words already in the title.

00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:51.400 align:start position:0%
Contrast matters more than colour when the image is that small.

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:56.900 align:start position:0%
Faces with one clear expression outperform crowded collages.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:03.700 align:start position:0%
Retention graphs show exactly where viewers abandon the video.

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:07.400 align:start position:0%
Export the audience retention chart from studio analytics.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:11.300 align:start position:0%
Steep cliffs mark moments, while slow slides mean pacing problems.

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:12.000 align:start position:0%
you know

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:16.100 align:start position:0%
Cut the middle instead of rewriting it when the slide is flat.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.000 align:start position:0%
Signpost every topic change so viewers know a payoff remains.

00:01:21.900 --> 00:01:25.600 align:start position:0%
Sponsor reads placed early create the deepest cliffs of all.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:30.000 align:start position:0%
Fix the biggest cliff first and ignore everything else this week.

